{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was born around 1140. His father was killed in 1152 and he succeeded him as the Count of Tripoli.\n\n*Early Life and Reign*\nRaymond III was still a minor when he succeeded his father. His mother Hodierna acted as regent for him until he came of age. In 1155 Raymond III was knighted by King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. He also married Eschiva of Bures in 1160.\n\nRaymond III had a difficult relationship with the Byzantine Empire. In 1164 he was taken prisoner by the Byzantine Emperor Manuel I Comnenus. He was released in 1165 after promising to provide military support to the Byzantines. However he failed to fulfill his promise and was forced to seek refuge in the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\n*Conflict with Saladin*\nRaymond III played a key role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187. He was one of the leaders of the Crusader army that was defeated by Saladin. After the battle Raymond III fled to Tyre where he died in 1187.\n\n*Succession and Legacy*\nRaymond III was succeeded by his godson Raymond of Antioch. However the County of Tripoli was eventually inherited by Bohemond IV of Antioch. Raymond III's legacy is complex and has been the subject of much debate among historians. Some view him as a weak and ineffective leader while others see him as a skilled diplomat and military commander.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004134069196879864}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.245502233505249}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.07054182887077332}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.015811331570148468}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576279254957626e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "